\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When wilt Thou save the people?
\par O God of mercy, when?
\par The people, Lord, the people,
\par Not thrones and crowns, but men!
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Flowers of Thy heart, O God, are they;
\par Let them not pass like weeds away,
\par Their heritage a sunless day.
\par God save the people!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Shall crime bring crime for ever,
\par Strength aiding still the strong?
\par Is it Thy will, O Father,
\par That man shall toil for wrong?
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par No! say Thy mountains: No! Thy skies;
\par Man's clouded sun shall brightly rise,
\par And songs be heard instead of sighs:
\par God save the people!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When wilt Thou save the people?
\par O God of mercy, when?
\par The people, Lord, the people,
\par Not thrones and crowns, but men!
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par God save the people; thine they are,
\par Thy children, as Thine angels fair;
\par From vice, oppression, and despair,
\par God save the people!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

